;; FH-BEHAVIOR-003 — the structural projection is an INERT MARKER, and the JVM
;; says so rather than pretending.
;;
;; A server has no live node, so a structural render connects nothing. What it
;; DOES do is record the whole public fact: the boundary node, the behavior's
;; registered id, the semantic target a command would address, and the public
;; config — with the author's own element as its child, unchanged. That is the
;; value below, pinned on both hosts.
;;
;; What is NOT in it is as load-bearing as what is: no node, no memory, no
;; cleanup handle, no host instance, no callback. The tree prints and reads back
;; losslessly, which is only true because the use site is data.
;;
;; The `:lifecycle` assertion is the other half — after rendering every view
;; here the lifecycle transcript is EMPTY. "Inert" is a claim about what did not
;; happen, so it is asserted as an absence.
;;
;; `:command` pins the JVM's answer to a command: the channel is a browser
;; capability, so a structural host REFUSES rather than silently doing nothing.
{:fh/id "FH-BEHAVIOR-003"
 :fh/law
 "On the structural host a behavior is an inert marker: the boundary node records the registered id, the semantic target and the public config with the decorated element as its child, no lifecycle runs at all, and a command is refused with the channel's own diagnostic rather than silently dropped."

 :lifecycle []

 :command
 {:frame   :structural/behaviors
  :args    {:target :probe/one :op :mark}
  :outcome :rf.error/behavior-command-refused}

 :cases
 [{:note "the ordinary attachment — id, target and public config, wrapping the author's element"
   :view :plain
   :args [{}]
   :tree {:view-id :re-frame.freehand.behavior-views/plain
          :children
          [{:tag :section :attrs {:class "host"}
            :children
            [{:view-id :re-frame.freehand/behavior
              :props   {:use    :re-frame.freehand.behavior-views/probe
                        :target :probe/one
                        :config {:label "a"}}
              :children [{:tag :div :attrs {:class "node"} :children ["content"]}]}]}]
          :rf.ui/tree-version 1}}

  {:note "no target is recorded as ABSENT, never as nil — a behavior nothing commands has none"
   :view :no-target
   :args [{}]
   :tree {:view-id :re-frame.freehand.behavior-views/no-target
          :children
          [{:view-id :re-frame.freehand/behavior
            :props   {:use    :re-frame.freehand.behavior-views/probe
                      :config {:label "quiet"}}
            :children [{:tag :div :attrs {:class "node"}}]}]
          :rf.ui/tree-version 1}}

  {:note "two occurrences project two markers, each carrying its own semantic id"
   :view :pair
   :args [{}]
   :tree {:view-id :re-frame.freehand.behavior-views/pair
          :children
          [{:tag :section :attrs {:class "host"}
            :children
            [{:view-id :re-frame.freehand/behavior
              :props   {:use    :re-frame.freehand.behavior-views/probe
                        :target :probe/one
                        :config {:label "one"}}
              :children [{:tag :div :attrs {:data-id "one" :class "node"}}]}
             {:view-id :re-frame.freehand/behavior
              :props   {:use    :re-frame.freehand.behavior-views/probe
                        :target :probe/two
                        :config {:label "two"}}
              :children [{:tag :div :attrs {:data-id "two" :class "node"}}]}]}]
          :rf.ui/tree-version 1}}]}
